---
import Project from '../../layouts/Project.astro';

const repo =
	'https://github.com/buragapuravi/ravikumarburagapu.com/tree/main/india-agricultural-evidence-assistant';
---

<Project
	title="India Agricultural Evidence Assistant"
	description="A local Agentic RAG workbench combining hybrid retrieval, a deterministic structured path, an evidence gate with abstention, and bounded multi-step planning over agricultural research documents."
	tag="AGENTIC RAG · HYBRID RETRIEVAL · EVIDENCE-FIRST"
	intro="A locally runnable workbench that shows what Agentic RAG, hybrid retrieval, and grounded LLM synthesis look like in practice—with every step inspectable. Ask a research question, watch the pipeline decide how to answer it, and trace every claim back to a cited passage or a validated source row."
	status="Local research demo · not an advisory service"
	stack="Python · Streamlit · LlamaIndex · Chroma · BM25 · Sentence Transformers · optional Ollama / OpenAI-compatible LLM"
	repo={repo}
>
	<section aria-labelledby="pipeline">
		<h2 id="pipeline">End-to-end pipeline</h2>
		<p>
			Every question passes through a deterministic routing and retrieval stack before
			an LLM is ever called—and a generation model is never required.
		</p>
		<ol>
			<li>
				<strong>Ingest.</strong> PDFs, Markdown, and UTF-8 text are chunked with
				heading- and paragraph-aware splitting. Each chunk carries source metadata
				(title, organization, page, crop, state, season). A SHA-256 manifest tracks
				ingestion state; model downloads are an explicit preparation step, not a
				hidden startup action.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Encode.</strong> A local multilingual Sentence Transformers model
				(<code>paraphrase-multilingual-MiniLM-L12-v2</code>) encodes chunks into
				vectors stored in a persistent Chroma collection. BM25 maintains a
				parallel lexical index over the same corpus.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Retrieve.</strong> Dense vector search and BM25 run independently.
				Reciprocal-rank fusion (RRF) merges the two candidate lists, applying 2×
				weight on lexical ranks to preserve exact agricultural terms and
				measurements. An optional cross-encoder reranks the fused list; if
				unavailable, fused ranking is used directly.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Gate.</strong> A deterministic evidence gate checks retrieval
				score, question-term coverage, missing crop/location/season context, source
				status, and advisory validity dates. A failed gate abstains rather than
				asking the LLM to fill gaps.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Synthesize.</strong> With <code>LLM_PROVIDER=none</code> (the
				default), the app returns a cited extractive passage with no model call.
				With a configured local or OpenAI-compatible provider, the prompt treats
				retrieved text as untrusted data and requests a grounded, cited answer.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Validate.</strong> Generated citation source IDs and page numbers
				are checked against retrieved chunks before display. Claims, passages, and
				retrieval diagnostics appear in separate inspectable panels.
			</li>
		</ol>
	</section>

	<section aria-labelledby="capabilities">
		<h2 id="capabilities">What this demo shows</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>Hybrid retrieval with an inspectable trace.</strong> Open the
				retrieval trace to see dense embedding candidates, BM25 candidates, the
				RRF merge, reranker state, and the evidence-gate decision for any query.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Deterministic structured path.</strong> Count and statistics
				questions route to validated CSV records—not vector search, not LLM
				arithmetic. The 23-district Punjab wheat/Rabi 2022–2023 comparison and
				ICAR extension indicators follow this path; provenance hashes and source
				links are always shown.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Evidence gate and abstention.</strong> The system declines to
				answer when support is insufficient, the question lacks required context,
				evidence conflicts, or an advisory is expired. This is the designed
				behavior, not a failure.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Bounded Agentic RAG.</strong> An optional LLM planner may propose
				at most two short follow-up searches; the original question always runs,
				so at most three read-only hybrid searches execute against the local index.
				The agent cannot browse the web, execute arbitrary code, or modify data.
				The trace exposes every plan query, tool call, and model call count—no
				hidden chain-of-thought.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Citation validation.</strong> Source IDs and page numbers generated
				by the LLM are validated against retrieved chunks before they reach the UI.
				Unsupported citations are dropped, not silently displayed.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Evaluation suite.</strong> An offline evaluation panel reports
				retrieval precision@5, recall@5, MRR, and nDCG@5 against curated relevant
				source IDs; abstention precision and recall; and citation coverage over
				answerable responses. Optional Ragas diagnostics (faithfulness, answer
				relevancy, context precision, context recall) require a configured
				LLM provider.
			</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<section aria-labelledby="scenarios">
		<h2 id="scenarios">Live demo scenarios</h2>
		<p>Six curated queries cover the main pipeline branches.</p>
		<dl>
			<div>
				<dt>"Which soil is good for rice crop?"</dt>
				<dd>
					Triggers rice/soil query expansion, hybrid retrieval, and the IRRI
					technical summary. Surfaces ~400 mm vs. 2,000+ mm seasonal water
					input across soil/groundwater conditions. Use the retrieval trace to
					walk through RRF and the evidence gate.
				</dd>
			</div>
			<div>
				<dt>"How many farmers attended the Bloomsdale rice field day, and how many were women?"</dt>
				<dd>
					Routes automatically to the structured ICAR indicator path. Returns
					43 participants, 32 women, 11 men, and a deterministically calculated
					74.4% women share—no vector search, no LLM arithmetic.
				</dd>
			</div>
			<div>
				<dt>"Which irrigation interval should cotton farmers in Maharashtra follow during kharif according to the demo notes?"</dt>
				<dd>
					The two bundled synthetic notes disagree. The expected behavior is
					abstention, not selecting one. Demonstrates conflict detection and the
					evidence gate declining to synthesize.
				</dd>
			</div>
			<div>
				<dt>"What should I spray to control pests in my farm?"</dt>
				<dd>
					Missing crop, location, and season context. The gate abstains and
					identifies the missing scope rather than inventing pesticide advice.
					Clear sidebar filters before running this one.
				</dd>
			</div>
			<div>
				<dt>"Compare wheat yields across Punjab districts for Rabi 2022–2023."</dt>
				<dd>
					Routes to the deterministic DES district comparison: 23 Punjab
					district rows, a chart/table, report-portal link, and row hashes.
					State, crop, and season filters must match the loaded extract.
				</dd>
			</div>
			<div>
				<dt>"Compare rice soil water requirements, explain how groundwater depth changes the comparison, and identify what evidence is still needed for a local soil-suitability decision."</dt>
				<dd>
					The optional Agentic RAG scenario (requires a configured LLM). Load
					scenario 06 and watch the bounded planner decompose the question,
					run up to three local searches, merge evidence, and validate citations.
				</dd>
			</div>
		</dl>
	</section>

	<section aria-labelledby="design">
		<h2 id="design">Technical design decisions</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>RRF over score normalization.</strong> Dense similarity scores and
				BM25 scores live on incompatible scales. Rank-based fusion avoids
				normalization assumptions while giving lexical retrieval extra weight to
				preserve exact crop names, measurement units, and program identifiers.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Deterministic arithmetic for numeric records.</strong> Asking an
				LLM to sum or divide reported counts introduces hallucination risk with no
				upside. Validated CSV rows with deterministic Python arithmetic are safer,
				faster, and cheaper for this class of question.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Bounded planner, not an autonomous agent.</strong> Unconstrained
				tool use amplifies hallucination risk and makes behavior hard to explain.
				A fixed upper bound on retrieval actions (original query + at most two
				follow-ups) keeps the trace readable and the demo reproducible.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Extractive-first, synthesis optional.</strong> The app returns
				cited passages without any generation model. Synthesis is an opt-in
				upgrade that must be explicitly configured; it does not change what
				evidence is available, only how it is presented.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Pluggable framework and storage.</strong> LlamaIndex (default)
				and LangChain adapters share the same Chroma collection and BM25 index,
				enabling a direct side-by-side framework comparison. pgvector is an
				optional drop-in backend for the same embedding contract.
			</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<section aria-labelledby="run">
		<h2 id="run">Run it locally</h2>
		<p>
			No paid API key required. The default <code>LLM_PROVIDER=none</code> returns
			cited extractive evidence without calling a generation model. Build the dense
			index from the included corpus:
		</p>
		<pre><code>cd india-agricultural-evidence-assistant
python3.12 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e '.[dev]'
cp .env.example .env
python -m app.prepare_models
python -m app.ingest --input data/demo --input data/raw --rebuild
streamlit run streamlit_app.py --server.address 127.0.0.1 --server.port 8502</code></pre>
		<p>
			To enable local LLM synthesis and the Agentic RAG planner, install and start
			Ollama, then set <code>LLM_PROVIDER=ollama</code> and <code>LLM_MODEL</code>
			in <code>.env</code>. For an OpenAI-compatible endpoint, set
			<code>LLM_PROVIDER=openai-compatible</code>, <code>LLM_BASE_URL</code>,
			and <code>LLM_MODEL</code>. Provider and model can also be overridden
			per-session under <strong>Advanced answer settings</strong> without editing
			<code>.env</code>.
		</p>
		<p>
			<a href={repo} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the full README</a>
			{' '}·{' '}
			<a href="/projects/research-chat">Chat with My Research (MCTS Agentic RAG)</a>
			{' '}·{' '}
			<a href="/projects/rag-judge-eval">Validated RAG Eval Harness</a>
		</p>
	</section>

	<section aria-labelledby="safety">
		<h2 id="safety">Scope and limitations</h2>
		<p>
			This is an evidence-discovery teaching prototype. The bundled documents are
			clearly labeled synthetic teaching fixtures and must never be used to make
			farming decisions. The app does not independently verify source authenticity,
			currentness, or agronomic correctness. Retrieval scores are diagnostic
			pipeline signals, not calibrated answer-confidence values. Abstention
			thresholds and conflict heuristics are demonstration starting points; real
			deployment requires domain expert review and a verified, current corpus.
		</p>
	</section>
</Project>

